      "originalReviewResult": "APPROVE_MINIMAL_FIX_SCOPE_PENDING_IMPLEMENTATION_AND_NATIVE_RECHECK",
      "observedBoundary": "All three status actions begin and return while this process is active/frontmost. Shortly after, popover.didShow records inactive/previous foreground application; willClose precedes the later-registered diagnostic didResignActive observer. The production control had registered an unconditional didResignActive close observer before the diagnostic observer.",
      "causalConfidence": "Source and timeline support an erroneous duplicate close on normal status-bar activation handback. Notification ordering alone is not a close-call stack and cannot prove the unique cause; the minimal patch must be checked in a real native run.",
      "approvedChange": "Remove only the resignObserver property, unconditional NSApplication.didResignActive registration, and corresponding deinit removal. Keep NSPopover.behavior transient and all explicit native close paths unchanged.",
      "preservedClosePaths": [
        "native transient handling of outside UI interaction",
        "existing app-local outside mouse events without swallowing/replaying events",
        "Escape",
        "second status-button click and pressBeganWhileShown handling",
        "settings/history/feedback/quit action closes before dispatch",
        "context-menu opening",
        "host.close teardown",
        "beginTerminationPreparation calls setInteractionSuspended(true), closes popover, disables status button and rejects stale commands"
      ],
      "verificationNeeded": [
        "Targeted notification regression should demonstrate that a posted resign notification alone no longer invokes this controller close path; retain the existing native status toggle and suspension tests. This is not proof of OS activation behavior.",
